    {
      "index": 0,
      "timestamp": "2026-09-14T02:55:58.878820Z",
      "thought": "The handover note says what was run and, more usefully, what was not: no prune, no clone, no fetch. That is the difference between a recovery and an apology.\n",
      "tool_name": "read_file",
      "tool_args": {
        "path": "README.md"
      },
      "tool_output": "# Handover note\n\n`repo/` is the feedloader checkout. `feature` was three commits of Priya's work on the\nvendor's rate limiting, branched off `main` before the CRLF change landed on it.\n\nI rebased it onto `main` this morning and deleted a line out of the todo list by mistake.\nThe branch came back with two commits on it instead of three. The one in the middle, the\nbackoff work, is not on the branch any more.\n\nThen I made it worse. While tidying up I ran\n\n    git reflog expire --expire-unreachable=now --all\n\nso the reflog no longer has the entry for where `feature` used to point. What I have not\ndone is run a garbage collection, and I have not cloned, pushed or fetched anything since,\nso whatever is left of that commit is still inside `repo/.git`. There is one copy of it.\nPlease read before you write.\n\nThere is no remote, no stash and no second checkout. Priya is out until Thursday, and the\ncommit is not on her machine either: she pushed it to this checkout and deleted her branch.\n\nWhat I need back: `feature` with its three commits, in the order they were written, sitting\non top of `main` where the rebase was trying to put them. Priya's commit has to still be\nher commit, with the same content, the same message, her name and her date on it. `main`\nhas not moved and should not.",
      "exit_code": null,
      "duration_ms": 0,
      "tokens_in": 372,
      "tokens_out": 44,
      "cost_usd": 0.0,
      "truncated": false,
      "schema_violation": false,
      "error": null,
      "failed": false
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "timestamp": "2026-09-14T02:55:58.902847Z",
      "thought": "Establish what is actually on the branch before believing any account of it. Two commits above main, both of Priya's outer two, and a clean tree.\n",
      "tool_name": "bash",
      "tool_args": {
        "command": "git -C repo log --oneline --graph --decorate --all | head -20\ngit -C repo status -sb\n"
      },
      "tool_output": "* 4c175d5 (HEAD -> feature) Put the fetch path behind the retry wrapper\n* 51ab2da Add a retry wrapper around the fetch step\n* abd7556 (main) Pin the feed record separator to CRLF\n* 6b4693a Add the CSV reader\n* ba8072c Add the feed fetcher\n## feature\n",
      "exit_code": 0,
      "duration_ms": 23,
      "tokens_in": 803,
      "tokens_out": 61,
      "cost_usd": 0.0,
      "truncated": false,
