    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "timestamp": "2026-09-14T02:55:58.984069Z",
      "thought": "Put a ref on it before doing anything else. Until something points at that commit it is one garbage collection away from gone, and the next few commands are exactly the sort that make git think about running one. Naming it first costs nothing and makes the rest of this reversible.\n",
      "tool_name": "bash",
      "tool_args": {
        "command": "lost=$(git -C repo fsck --dangling --no-progress | awk '/dangling commit/{print $3; exit}')\ngit -C repo branch rescue \"$lost\"\ngit -C repo log --oneline --decorate rescue | head\n"
      },
      "tool_output": "8a17123 (rescue) Put the fetch path behind the retry wrapper\nac73d68 Back off when the vendor answers 429\nb78dc75 Add a retry wrapper around the fetch step\n6b4693a Add the CSV reader\nba8072c Add the feed fetcher\n",
      "exit_code": 0,
