      "thought": "Read what was found before rebuilding anything on it. Three commits of Priya's, and the middle one is the backoff work with her name and her date on it, touching src/retry.py and adding a test.\n",
      "tool_name": "bash",
      "tool_args": {
        "command": "git -C repo log --format='%h %an <%ae> %aI %s' -3 rescue\ngit -C repo show --stat --format='%n%H%nauthor %an %aI%n%n%s%n' rescue~1\n"
      },
      "tool_output": "8a17123 Priya Raman <priya@example.com> 2026-02-12T14:03:47+00:00 Put the fetch path behind the retry wrapper\nac73d68 Priya Raman <priya@example.com> 2026-02-11T09:14:22+00:00 Back off when the vendor answers 429\nb78dc75 Priya Raman <priya@example.com> 2026-02-10T08:55:13+00:00 Add a retry wrapper around the fetch step\n\nac73d68f023769dd4380404f30067bc2e58b60b1\nauthor Priya Raman 2026-02-11T09:14:22+00:00\n\nBack off when the vendor answers 429\n\n\n src/retry.py          | 20 +++++++++++++++++---\n tests/test_backoff.py | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\n",
      "exit_code": 0,
